Nice one. With `['int', 'string']` and a string, resolving 20 options goes from 29 µs to 19 µs here.

The most common order in our form types is `['null', ...]` though (28 times), and `null` isn't in `VALIDATION_FUNCTIONS`, so it still takes the slow path. What about short-circuiting any plain type name instead? This takes `['null', 'string']` from 34 µs to 20 µs:

```php
if ('callable' !== $type && false === strpbrk($type, "|()[] \t\n\r\0\x0B")) {
    if (\is_array($invalidTypes) && (!$invalidTypes || $level > 0)) {
        $invalidTypes[get_debug_type($value)] = true;
    }

    return false;
}
```

